{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_019mGP394eqb8UjMubJWKXzi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TcgZFRXHFjz8JRswgSdE2b","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\Johan\\Desktop\\KonsiliTradingview\\analysis_journal\\SOLUSDT_2026-05-17_hew\\journal.md","content":"# SOLUSDT 2026-05-17 — Ian Copsey / Fractal Forecasting\n\n## Verdict\n\n**STAND ASIDE.** Confidence: **very_low**. Package validity: **fail**. Evidence grade: **failed**. Trade permission: **blocked**.\n\n## Why\n\nTwo blockers force the call:\n\n1. **Konsili Pivot Exporter data-path failure.** The KPE indicator is attached on the chart (entity id `TR8cKk`, listed by `chart_get_state` on Monthly, Weekly, and Daily). But `data_get_pine_tables` and `data_get_pine_labels` returned `study_count=0` on all three timeframes, both with and without `study_filter=\"Konsili Pivot Exporter\"`, before and after removing and re-attempting the indicator. No KPE row could be harvested. Per `strategies/hew/manifest.json` and `AGENTS.md`, this is a pivot data-path failure. KPE rows must not be fabricated. Confidence is capped to `very_low` and trade language is blocked.\n\n2. **OHLCV-only macro Wave 3 fails the Copsey 1.764 floor.** Using the OHLCV-derived swings as fallback context only (not promoted as a count), Macro Wave 3 measures (295.83 − 8.00) / (259.90 − 1.0301) = 287.83 / 258.87 = **1.112×** Wave 1. That fails the default hard floor of 1.764. No rare exception is documented because the broader Copsey evidence base is missing (no KPE pivots, no verifiable internal subwave proof). The honest call is `STAND ASIDE`.\n\nNo classical Elliott rescue device is used to save the failed Wave 3. No native Elliott drawings were placed on the chart because anchoring counts to unverified pivots would breach the manifest's `point_locking` requirement. Konsili Castaway is treated as an overlay only and does not rewrite the count.\n\n## Method\n\nIan Copsey / Fractal Forecasting on `BINANCE:SOLUSDT`. Macro-first read on Monthly → Weekly → Daily; no execution-timeframe work because the macro is unresolved.\n\n## Active count and alternate\n\nThis run does **not** promote a primary or alternate Copsey count to actionable status because the pivot data-path failed. The OHLCV-only fallback narrative — for diagnostic context only — is:\n\n- **Fallback macro context:** 1.03 (2020-12) → 259.90 (2021-11) → 8.00 (2022-12) → 295.83 (2025-01) → 67.50 (2026-02) → 86.91 (current). Wave 3 fails the floor.\n- **Alternate context (super-cycle):** the entire 2020–2025 advance could be one super-cycle Wave 1 and 2026 action is Wave 2; this can only be tested with verified KPE pivots.\n- **Rejected:** the active rebound 67.50 → ~98 is structurally too small (≈8.5% of the prior swing) to claim impulse status.\n\n## Zones (uncalibrated, fallback-derived scores)\n\n| Zone | Type | Range | Score | Band |\n|------|------|-------|-------|------|\n| Lower accumulation | accumulation | 67.50 – 86.91 | 30 | moderate_low |\n| Deeper accumulation | accumulation | 33.00 – 67.50 | 25 | moderate_low |\n| Near distribution | distribution | 98.41 – 148.74 | 55 | moderate |\n| Upper distribution | distribution | 187.21 – 253.51 | 45 | moderate |\n\nAll scores capped low because KPE path failed; distribution score exceeds the highest accumulation score, which is consistent with `STAND ASIDE`.\n\n## Invalidation and flip\n\nOuter invalidation defined on the OHLCV fallback only:\n- Weekly acceptance below **67.50** ends the lower accumulation read and shifts attention to the deeper accumulation band.\n- Monthly close below **33.00** cancels the deeper accumulation read.\n- Weekly acceptance above **148.74** would reduce the near-distribution dominance.\n- Weekly acceptance above **253.51** would reduce the upper-distribution band.\n\n## Target path\n\nNo verifiable target path while the KPE pivot data path is down and the OHLCV Wave 3 floor fails. The 187.21–253.51 band is recorded as **potential distribution**, not as an entry target.\n\n## Review conditions\n\n- KPE Pine MCP reads return valid `KPE|...` rows on Monthly, Weekly, and Daily → re-run the full workflow with verified pivots.\n- Price tests the 67.50 floor or the 33.00 deeper-accumulation band → refresh accumulation score on a verified-pivot path.\n- Price enters 98.41 – 148.74 or 187.21 – 253.51 → refresh distribution score on a verified-pivot path.\n\n## What to do nothing on\n\n- Do nothing on the rebound from 67.50 toward the 98 area as a \"reversal.\" It is too small structurally and the Wave 3 floor fails on the OHLCV fallback.\n- Do not draw a Copsey wave map from OHLCV-only pivots. The manifest requires `point_locking` to KPE source rows and an OHLCV check ID; that cannot be satisfied this run.\n\n## Chart state left behind\n\nWeekly `BINANCE:SOLUSDT` on `Hew Layout`, Awesome Oscillator visible, Konsili Pivot Exporter and Pivot Points High Low hidden, **no drawings** (intentional). `raw/chart_state_final.json` captures the exact state.\n\n## Files\n\n- `journal.md` (this file)\n- `evidence.json`\n- `committee_brief.md`\n- `screenshots/visual_pivots_monthly.png`\n- `screenshots/visual_pivots_weekly.png`\n- `screenshots/visual_pivots_daily.png`\n- `screenshots/macro_structure.png`\n- `screenshots/trade_posture.png`\n- `raw/kpe_monthly.jsonl` (data-path-failure record)\n- `raw/kpe_weekly.jsonl` (data-path-failure record)\n- `raw/kpe_daily.jsonl` (data-path-failure record)\n- `raw/ohlcv_monthly.csv`\n- `raw/ohlcv_weekly.csv`\n- `raw/ohlcv_daily.csv`\n- `raw/draw_list_before.json` (empty)\n- `raw/draw_list_after.json` (empty)\n- `raw/chart_state_final.json`\n- `raw/hashes.json`\n\n## Required follow-ups\n\n1. Restore Konsili Pivot Exporter Pine table/label MCP visibility for `BINANCE:SOLUSDT`.\n2. Re-extract KPE pivots on Monthly, Weekly, and Daily once MCP path is restored.\n3. Re-run the HEW workflow with verified pivots before any actionable la